                <pb facs="0762" n="650" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg650"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 25010/24.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Italian Chargé to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Italian Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Manchester,
                                Mass.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1910-06-27"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">June 27,
                    1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Urgent. Judge Blair insists on having preliminary mandate prescribed in article 2
                    of convention of 1884, so as to maintain arrest of Porter Charlton. I beg you,
                    your excellency, to urgently send me or directly to Italian consul. New York,
                    the said document, so that arrest of murderer be maintained until a decision can
                    be taken on the question.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Montagliari.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
